  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed additional storey by reason of its scale, siting and design would be a visually prominent, intrusive and incongruous form of development that would fail to appear suitably subservient or relate sympathetically to the character and appearance of the existing property, streetscene or the adjacent Wandsworth Common Conservation Area. Furthermore, the scale and prominent location of the proposed waste storage provision would detrimentally impact the appearance of the streetscene. The proposal therefore fails to comply with the NPPF (2024), policies LP1, LP3, LP5 and LP7 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023) and the guidance within the Housing SPD (2016). ",
    "Reason : 2 - By reason of the insufficient size of the private amenity space provided for the new flats, the proposed development would afford future occupiers with a poor standard of accommodation. Furthermore, the application has also failed to demonstrate that the proposed flat would be provided with acceptable internal floor to ceiling heights. As such, the development fails the requirements of policies LP27 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023), policy D6 of the London Plan (2021) and the Technical Housing Standards - Nationally Described Space Standard (2015).",
    "Reason : 3 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to make available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal."
  ],
